{"id": "13277142181", "client": "curegrin", "eyebrow": "CureGRIN · NYC Pharma Day, GRIN Therapeutics · 8 Oct 2026 · Social cut", "title": "Keith McArthur:", "title_q": "“The Seventh Family”", "title_short": "Keith McArthur · The Seventh Family", "editor": "Ardit", "due": "2026-10-26", "format": "9:16 only · 1080×1920", "length": "about 45 s", "edit_key": "CureGRINSeventhFamily001", "headline": "A family waits almost 10 years for a name for their son's condition. Then they find six other families. Today there are hundreds.", "story": ["Keith tells his family story to the staff of GRIN Therapeutics at lunch. The test that was never sent. Almost 10 years to a diagnosis. The question every parent asks. Then a Facebook group with six other families. <b>Community is the lifeline.</b> It is not about science, the drug or the meeting. The end is hope.", "<b>Loops:</b> L1 “What test, and for who?” opens 0:00 and closes at 0:07. L2 “Were they alone with this?” opens 0:00 and closes in the button. <b>Stakes:</b> a family waits almost 10 years to learn what their son has."], "feel": ["Hopeful", "Personal", "Warm", "Simple"], "do": ["Open on Keith's face, already talking, with the hook text.", "One thought per cut. Keep his pauses short.", "Crop to 9:16 on Keith. He stands on the right in most clips.", "Small name super at 0:07, lower left, 2 seconds.", "Hold one second on the last line."], "dont": ["No logo, name or fade at 0:00.", "Never say or show that GRI disorders can be prevented, that a cure is near, or that anyone is at fault.", "Do not show the Zoom name tiles on the lunch room TV. Crop or blur them.", "No close shots of slides with data, except the ones named here.", "Never use the words “find your hive”."], "links": {"brief": {"title": "CureGRIN NYC Pharma Partnership Prod Brief v2", "url": "https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HL-hpEXriFw2NHjXlxFpkwxMajQPKg1qLCqQIqfks88/edit", "note": "The production brief of the 8 Oct shoot day."}, "reference": {"missing": true, "ti