 as a child. You can slide the crop to the photo for 2 seconds.", "motion": "<b>Name super</b> at <span class=\"mono\">00:07</span>, small, lower left, 2 seconds: <q>Keith McArthur</q> / <q>CureGRIN</q>. Loop 1 closes here.", "voice": {"who": "Keith McArthur", "quote": "So that kind of led to what often gets referred to as a diagnostic odyssey. And ours was long. So Bryson didn't get his diagnosis till he was almost 10 years old.", "src": "20261008_C5194 00:03.0 to 00:13.0"}, "sfx": "<span class=\"none\">None.</span>", "music": "Bed steady, low."}, {"tc": "00:17-00:28", "beat": "THE QUESTION", "kind": "", "frame": "f_C5197_36", "crop": "r", "frame_tag": "src 0:36", "frame_alt": "Wide shot. Keith stands on the right of a TV with a slide.", "visual": "<a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Yh8DoDwrfMddd2pdzosRhlw_Ld6Sy6zB/view\">20261008_C5197.MP4</a> from <span class=\"mono\">00:34</span>. Wide shot, Keith on the right side of frame. Crop in on Keith.", "motion": "Captions only.", "voice": {"who": "Keith McArthur", "quote": "is it degenerative? So the key thing we really wanted to know is what she meant by that is, is Bryson gonna die from this? Is he gonna die from this soon? And she basically just said, we don't think so.", "src": "20261008_C5197 00:34.6 to 00:45.2"}, "sfx": "<span class=\"none\">None.</span>", "music": "Music thinner here."}, {"tc": "00:28-00:38", "beat": "SIX OTHER FAMILIES", "kind": "", "frame": "f_C5198_36", "crop": "r", "frame_tag": "src 0:36", "frame_alt": "Medium shot of Keith on the right. A TV with Zoom tiles on the left.", "visual": "<a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Sg8R5rgjK2dW4U0F1N1vFWhsVk5MuARs/view\">20261008_C5198.MP4</a> from <span class=\"mono\">00:32</span>. Medium shot of Keith, he stands on the right.", "motion": "Captions only.", "voice": {"who": "Keith McArthur", "quote": "So from that, we found a Facebook group that at the time had six other families. We were the seventh to join this Facebook group of GRIN1 families around the world.", "src": "20261008_C5198 00:32.9 to 00:42.3"}, "sfx": "<span class=\"none\">None.</span>", "music": "Bed steady, low."}, {"tc": "00:38-00:40", "beat": "BUTTON", "kind": "turn", "frame": null, "crop": "none", "frame_tag": null, "frame_alt": null, "visual": "Same clip, <span class=\"mono\">00:44.5</span>. Hold one second.", "motion": "Captions only. Loop 2 closes here.", "voice": {"who": "Keith McArthur", "quote": "Now there are hundreds in that group.", "src": "20261008_C5198 00:44.5 to 00:46.0"}, "sfx": "<span class=\"none\">None.</span>", "music": "Small lift."}, {"tc": "00:40-00:45", "beat": "END CARD", "kind": "end", "frame": null, "crop": "none", "frame_tag": null, "frame_alt": null, "visual": "End card. The logo is here only.", "motion": "<q>Support CureGRIN today.</q> and <q>curegrin.org</q>.", "voice": "<span class=\"none\">No voice.</span>", "sfx": "<span class=\"none\">None.</span>", "music": "Music only. Warm. Resolve and fade 1 s."}], "frames": {"f_C5195_still": "data:image/jpeg;base64,", "f_C5194_6": "data:image/jpeg;base64,", "f_C5197_36": "data:image/jpeg;base64,", "f_C5198_36": "data:image/jpeg;base64,"}, "files": [["Monday brief", "<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Jwzf_3SkcMEaS_g0LvV-kv_09Rtzo9oRGRfWgDv1SfY/edit\">Editing brief (Google Doc)</a>"], ["Production brief", "<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HL-hpEXriFw2NHjXlxFpkwxMajQPKg1qLCqQIqfks88/edit\">CureGRIN NYC Pharma Partnership Prod Brief v2</a>"], ["Reference", "Not chosen yet. Nick owes it."], ["Shoot folder", "<a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/16HOlmEbUhY99EQQHsC31N2xwTwzhISMT\">CureGRIN NYC OCT 2026</a>"], ["Clips", "<a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/15KfsRUBBTMSX-M_arC9I_bXUHWke5s7b/view\">20261008_C5195.MP4</a> · <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/15REHTEQNMUthYGrNAl0_F_3WZDyGFB_q/view\">20261008_C5194.MP4</a> · <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Yh8DoDwrfMddd2pdzosRhlw_Ld6Sy6zB/view\">20261008_C5197.MP4</a> · <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Sg8R5rgjK2dW4U0F1N1vFWhsVk5MuARs/view\">20261008_C5198.MP4</a> · folder Keith Lunch Presentation"], ["Spare bite", "20261008_C5194 00:45.9 to 00:53.9: “And for each test that they did, it caused so much fear for my wife and I.”"], ["Transcript", "<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iR6tmLR8zlWn1EPcMxjVz5mTmwPfhbqTebbXteNpwoo/edit\">Transcripts - Keith Lunch Presentation</a> · the folder also has transcript.json with word times"], ["visual.json", "No separate file. The shot notes are inside transcript.json in each EditingResources folder."], ["Moving portrait", "None found in the folders. Do not look for it."], ["Music", "Warm and quiet, under the voice."]], "tech": [["Source", "Two cameras, both 1920×1080. Files named 20261008_C5… (the lunch talk, the morning B-roll, Bruce front angle): <b>59.94 fps</b>. Files named C48… (Keith front angle, Bruce side angle): <b>23.976 fps</b>. Measured on C5224, C5195, C5186, C4898 and C4896. Check the other files on import. Audio: 2 channels, recorded into the camera."], ["Timeline", "1080×1920 at <b>23.976 fps</b>. Conform the 59.94 clips to 23.976."], ["Crop", "The source is 1080p. A 9:16 crop is an upscale of about 178%. Do not punch in more than that. Use the two angles for variety."], ["Audio", "Keith wears a lav at lunch. Two camera channels. The audio check did not run. On scrub, find the channel with the lav and use it on both sides."], ["Loudness", "-14 LUFS integrated, -1 dBTP peak. Music well under the voice."], ["Captions", "Burned in from the first word to the last. Brand purple pill style, same as the GRIN2B cuts. Spellings: CureGRIN, GRIN1, GRI disorders, GRIN Therapeutics, radiprodil, Beeline, Bryson."], ["Export", "H.264 MP4, 1080×1920, 9:16. Upload to Frame.io → Ready for Review."]], "checklist": ["Frame 1 is Keith's face, already talking, with the hook text. No logo, name or fade.", "The hook text is on screen at 0:00 and does not animate on.", "The name super comes at 0:07, not before 0:03.", "No Zoom name tile can be read in any shot.", "Bryson and GRIN1 are spelled right in the captions.", "The last line is “Now there are hundreds in that group.”", "The end card says “Support CureGRIN today.” and curegrin.org. The logo is only there.", "The file is 9:16 only."], "decisions": [{"t": "Reference", "b": "No visual reference is chosen for this shoot. Nick owes it."}, {"t": "Approval before publishing", "b": "Staff of GRIN Therapeutics are in the shots. Nick sends each cut to GRIN Therapeutics for approval before CureGRIN publishes it."}, {"t": "Names and titles", "b": "Quinn confirms every name and title before captions lock. The client file spells it Keith McArthur. The Drive folder says MacArthur."}], "client_note": "<b>Why this matters:</b> these films are for big donors and partners. They show a small family foundation as a real partner of a drug company.", "ask_examples": ["Where does Keith talk about the Facebook group?", "Can I show the photo of Bryson on the TV?", "What is the spare bite?", "Who approves this cut before it is published?"], "transcript": "--- 20261008_C5195.MP4 (times are mm:ss in this file)\n[00:00] I'm 12 years old, I think, because I've\n[00:02] been treated by gene therapy.\n[00:05] But that was something that Bryson was tested for.\n[00:08] And we looked it up online and saw how serious it was.\n[00:11] And we saw that kids were dying before they were two.\n[00:15] And we had to wait for three months\n[00:17] for the tests to come back.\n[00:19] And after four or five months, my wife\n[00:22] called up the children's hospital\n[00:25] and said, shouldn't we be getting our tests back by now?\n[00:27] Like they said, three months.\n[00:29] The person on the phone, I think it was a nurse,\n[00:32] was like, no, no, we'll call you when they come in.\n[00:34] Don't worry.\n[00:35] And a couple more months went by, and she called again.\n[00:38] And she looked into it and realized\n[00:40] that the tests had never actually been sent out.\n--- 20261008_C5194.MP4 (times are mm:ss in this file)\n[00:00] the actual cause.\n[00:02] So that kind of led to what often gets\n[00:05] referred to as a diagnostic odyssey.\n[00:08] And ours was long.\n[00:09] So Bryson didn't get his diagnosis\n[00:11] till he was almost 10 years old.\n[00:14] We had a couple of MRIs.\n[00:18] He had a biopsy to try to determine\n[00:20] if the low muscle tone was in his muscles or in his brain.\n[00:23] And his muscles turned out to be normal.\n[00:25] His brain looked normal on the MRI.\n[00:28] So we did a number of different first individual tests\n[00:32] for specific disorders, then for panels.\n[00:39] But what ultimately gave us the diagnosis\n[00:41] was a whole exome sequence.\n[00:43] And he didn't get till he was almost 10.\n[00:45] And for each test that they did, it\n[00:49] caused so much fear for my wife and I.\n[00:54] And so one example is.\n--- 20261008_C5197.MP4 (times are mm:ss in this file)\n[00:00] in Toronto and so he continues to be a physician for Bryson,\n[00:06] but he's also someone very, obviously,\n[00:08] very important to that system.\n[00:12] So eventually we got this call, my wife got a call\n[00:15] that they wanted to set up an appointment with us\n[00:18] because they had found something in the genetics report\n[00:21] and the person who called actually was the genetic counselor\n[00:25] and she said, well can you tell us what it is?\n[00:27] She's like, no, let's wait for the appointment,\n[00:28] it'll be the geneticist who tells you what it is,\n[00:31] but I'll be there.\n[00:32] And my wife just said, well can you tell us,\n[00:34] is it degenerative?\n[00:35] So the key thing we really wanted to know\n[00:38] is what she meant by that is,\n[00:39] is Bryson gonna die from this?\n[00:41] Is he gonna die from this soon?\n[00:43] And she basically just said, we don't think so.\n[00:45] So we both felt quite relieved to learn that.\n--- 20261008_C5198.MP4 (times are mm:ss in this file)\n[00:00] were a handful of patients who had been diagnosed.\n[00:04] And so on the way home, usually my wife always likes to drive.\n[00:07] She likes to be in control, so she drives.\n[00:09] But this day, she asked me to drive.\n[00:11] And so she was googling GRIN1.\n[00:14] And at the time, these were the top results\n[00:16] that came up, which were all publications about GRIN1\n[00:20] related to schizophrenia.\n[00:21] So we were like, is this connected to schizophrenia?\n[00:25] Because there had been very few publications at the time\n[00:27] about it being a monogenic disorder.\n[00:32] So from that, we found a Facebook group that at the time\n[00:36] had six other families.\n[00:38] We were the seventh to join this Facebook group of GRIN1\n[00:40] families around the world.\n[00:44] Now there are hundreds in that group."}